    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lean heavily into **Gunnar Henderson** (78.38) today, as his favorable matchup against Kremer and the premier lead-off spot make him our undeniable anchor. Alongside him, **Kyle Tucker** (67.24) serves as a primary source of high-floor production, benefiting from favorable wind conditions against Cameron. We are also prioritizing **Jacob Wilson** (63.17) and **Andy Pages** (62.44); **Jacob Wilson** leverages a strong park factor and a solid order position to overcome the threat posed by Peralta, while **Andy Pages** enjoys an additional boost from projected winds blowing out, maximizing his scoring potential despite Cameron\u2019s mid-tier xERA.\n\nTactical adjustments remain fluid, particularly with several lineups still pending. **Drake Baldwin** (53.73) carries the highest risk/reward profile today, as his strong lead-off assignment is clouded by a 37% rain risk. He remains in the starting lineup despite the weather because his xwOBA profile is too strong to ignore. Meanwhile, the most difficult decision on the bench involved **Wade Meckler** (38.79). While **Wade Meckler** offered potential utility, the optimizer ultimately favored the superior baseline projections and order placement of our starters. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, all of whom are unavailable today due to injury or scheduling, and we remain ready to pivot if the final lineups for **Liam Hicks**, **Andy Pages**, or **Kyle Tucker** shift unfavorably. Our bench depth, including **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara**, is currently set aside to preserve our game caps as we wait for more advantageous matchups.",
